WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.410
This ledger keeps 125 open-source AI tools.

2
00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:12.167
Each one has a grade, from E zero to E five. The grade counts proof, not popularity.

3
00:00:12.567 --> 00:00:17.561
E zero means we only read about it. 103 tools are there.

4
00:00:17.561 --> 00:00:22.326
To move up, a tool has to do real work in a named project.

5
00:00:22.726 --> 00:00:28.104
Take the voice you are hearing. It recorded the narration of this ledger's story video.

6
00:00:28.104 --> 00:00:32.727
That use was written down: the task, the result, and what went wrong.

7
00:00:32.727 --> 00:00:39.168
A person read the record and approved the move to E one. 16 tools are at E one.

8
00:00:39.568 --> 00:00:45.340
E two asks for more. The expected result is written down before the tool runs.

9
00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:51.688
A text reader was asked to read 32 headlines from a video. It read 32 of 32.

10
00:00:51.688 --> 00:00:55.603
A second reader, on the same images, read 28.

11
00:00:55.603 --> 00:00:59.717
6 tools have reached E two. None is higher yet.

12
00:01:00.117 --> 00:01:07.382
A check can also fail. A skill scanner was expected to give 5 known verdicts. It got 3 of 5.

13
00:01:07.382 --> 00:01:13.683
That result is kept. The scanner stays at E one, and a second scanner was built here.

14
00:01:14.083 --> 00:01:18.204
Only recorded use and a person's approval move a grade.

15
00:01:18.204 --> 00:01:24.488
125 tools. 22 did real work. 74 uses on record.

16
00:01:24.488 --> 00:01:27.582
This is the Tool Research Ledger.
